course: dictionary
lesson: 3718
title: Flicker: light and movement
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A flicker is a light or movement that keeps changing: it is there, then gone, then back again. You can use the words around a word to work out its meaning. «It is like a moth flying across a distant lighthouse: you cannot see the moth, but the light flickers.» The light is changing quickly, so flicker must mean to shine unsteadily.
explain: Look at the clues. The moth is hard to see, yet the light still keeps changing. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Light that gets brighter and dimmer again and again is a flicker, so the word fits.
explain: Flicker also works for movement and feelings. A flicker of hope is a small, sudden feeling that comes and goes. The words small and sudden tell you it is brief, not big and steady.
fact: To flicker means to shine unsteadily, getting brighter and dimmer quickly, like a candle flame.
fact: To flicker can also mean to move quickly and lightly, like eyelids or a shadow.
fact: A flicker is a quick, unsteady light or movement, or a small sudden feeling.
fact: «A flicker of hope» means a small, brief feeling of hope.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence: «the lights flickered» still makes sense if you say the lights shone unsteadily.
exercise: Ben says flicker means to stay still and steady. What does flicker really mean? | *Move or shine quickly and unsteadily | Move slowly and stay in one place | Fall to the ground | Shine steadily for hours
exercise: «It is like a moth flying across a distant lighthouse: you cannot see the moth, but the light flickers.» What does flickers mean here? | Stays perfectly still and steady | Makes a loud buzzing noise | *Shines unsteadily, getting brighter and dimmer | Goes out for ever
exercise: «A flicker of hope» means | A big, steady wave of joy | A loud noise in the night | *A small, sudden feeling that comes and goes | A bright, shiny coin
test: «The lights flickered» in the dark house. What does flickered mean? | Fell down from the ceiling | Went out completely and stayed dark | Stayed bright and steady all night | *Shone unsteadily, brighter then dimmer
test: In «a flicker of a smile», what does the word flicker show? | *A small, brief feeling hidden behind the face | A long, deep sleep | A broken window | A huge laugh that lasts all day
exam: In «her eyelids flickered», what does flickered mean? | To grow very large and round | To make a loud noise | *To move quickly and lightly | To shut tightly and stay shut
